      },
      "lineNbr": 392,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001923
      },
      "writtenOn": "2012-07-26T00:35:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The while() certainly can go.\n\nI actually tested it without the condition here and it works just fine without it (since the select_column always just sets stuff to Hi-Z when scanning is disabled).  I thought it\u0027d be good to have in there so it doesn\u0027t keep re-setting the whole keyboard matrix to Hi-Z over and over again, which seemed rather silly.  I\u0027m not sure what trumps in a situation like this, should we go with what makes the code simpler or the saved running time?",
